index 966937b..48f858d 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -305,6 +305,13 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 path. The controller classifies that submitted slash-prefixed chat text as a provider-native command
 for the selected agent session.
 
+In command mode, `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start character, line, and block visual selections in the
+focused pane. Visual movement accepts `h/j/k/l` and terminal arrow keys, and visual-mode escape
+sequence parsing keeps bytewise CSI arrow input inside the selection state until the full key is
+known. `y` copies the selected text, `Y` copies linewise text, and command-mode `Y` copies the
+focused line. Copies are stored in `TerminalUi` for tests and emitted through OSC 52 so compatible
+terminals receive the selected text on the system clipboard.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
